cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis, its data tables, or its code, please cite it as below, and cite the survey data too."
type: software
title: "May ponds and breeding ducks in Prairie Canada, 1955 to 2026"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
authors:
  - family-names: "Wootton"
    given-names: "Eric"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ericwootton/prairie-ducks"
url: "https://ericwootton.github.io/prairie-ducks/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An analysis of the Waterfowl Breeding Population and Habitat Survey for the 15
  Prairie Canada strata, 1955 to 2026. Hierarchical generalized additive models
  estimate how strongly breeding numbers of five dabbling ducks and canvasback
  follow May ponds, whether that response has changed over time, and what a
  given loss of ponds implies for breeding ducks. The code is MIT licensed; the
  derived tables, figures, and text are CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - waterfowl
  - prairie pothole region
  - wetland loss
  - northern pintail
  - generalized additive models
  - WBPHS
references:
  - type: data
    title: "WBPHS Traditional Survey Area Population Estimates, 1955 to Present"
    authors:
